+### H3.6 — End-to-end lattice pipeline: wiring truncation, rotation, and ratchet into a real score
+
+- **Hypothesis:** the double-lattice backbone, with nearest-candidate
+  truncation, global-rotation search, and a downward ratchet, produces a
+  combined score (n=1..200) well under the M3 target of ≤ 110.
+- **Kind:** empirical; label: `reference/evaluator.py` score, zero overlaps,
+  clearance ≥ `CLEARANCE_EPS`.
+- **Pipeline (in order):**
+  1. M2 best placements for n=1..20 loaded from `artifacts/best_scores.json`.
+  2. For n=21..200: `truncate_to_n(BASIS, n)` (H3.3 nearest-candidate
+     window) → `best_rotation` (H2 global rotation search over [0°, 90°)).
+  3. Fast arithmetic ratchet (see below) sweeping n=199 down to 21.
+- **Known-good lattice used (H3.2 seed 4):**
+  `LatticeBasis(p=0.8466998057329839, q=-0.2595569327159729,
+  h=0.8000013958277571, u=-0.15564510572139056, v=-0.30308104064715025)`,
+  cell density 0.725241, verified feasible and overlap-free.
+
+**Real numbers (all computed this session, not estimated):**
+
+| Stage | n=1..20 | n=21..200 | Total |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| M2 baseline | 17.7076 | — | — |
+| Lattice + rotation (pre-ratchet) | — | 83.2759 | 100.9835 |
+| After fast ratchet (38 improvements) | — | 82.5797 | **100.2873** |
+
+**M3 target ≤ 110: MET. Final total = 100.2873.**
