+
+**Performance bug found and fixed (fast arithmetic ratchet):**
+
+The existing `ratchet_layouts` in
+`src/tree_packing/optimize/postprocess/ratchet.py` calls `evaluate_layout`
+for every trial removal, which does full Shapely polygon construction, a
+`unary_union` bounding-box call, and an STRtree clearance scan — making each
+trial O(n) in Shapely time. Over a full n=21..200 pass with n+1 trial
+removals each, this is ≈20,000 Shapely calls: ~15-20 minutes total.
+
+The fix (from H3.3b's insight): each tree's bounding box is a fixed offset
+from its center at a given rotation angle. Bounding box of the whole layout
+is therefore just componentwise min/max over cached per-angle offsets — pure
+arithmetic, no geometry library. Offset table is warm after one Shapely call
+per unique angle (52 angles in this run). Result: ratchet completes in
+**2.6 seconds** instead of ~15-20 minutes. Accuracy cross-check against
+`evaluate_layout` for n=172,180,190,200 shows ≤ 5×10⁻¹⁶ Decimal difference
+(floating-point noise, not a real gap).
+
